# =============================================================================
# Mahaa backend — Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The rule: the build context must never carry a real secret, a virtualenv, a
# local cache or a development-only tree into the image. Everything below is
# excluded on purpose; `app/`, `alembic/`, `alembic.ini`, `requirements.txt` and
# `pyproject.toml` are deliberately NOT listed, so the runtime image can import
# the application and run migrations.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# A real `.env` must never be baked into a layer: it would be readable from the
# image by anyone who can pull it, and it stays in history forever.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# `.env.*` above also matches the committed template. That file is a safe set of
# placeholders with no real credential in it, so it is kept in the context on
# purpose: negation applies last, so this rule wins over the exclusions above.
!.env.example

# --- virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
# A Windows/macOS `.venv` is unusable inside a Linux image and is hundreds of MB.
.venv/
venv/

# --- python bytecode and tooling caches --------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- development-only trees --------------------------------------------------
# The suite and the tooling scripts are not runtime dependencies. The Dockerfile
# copies named paths anyway, so these are belt-and-braces against a future
# `COPY . .`.
tests/
tools/

# --- local database artefacts and logs ---------------------------------------
# A local scratch database or a pg_dump must never ride along into a layer.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

*.dump
*.log

# --- version control and editor cruft ----------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore

# --- frontend / node artefacts (not used by the API image) -------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/